  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe figurative sense (sense 2) is very common. {喜|よろこ}びを{噛|か}みしめる (to savor one's joy) is a set phrase. The metaphor of \"chewing\" to mean deep reflection is natural and productive in Japanese.\n\nIchidan verb ({一段動詞|いちだんどうし}).\n- Negative: {噛|か}みしめない\n- Polite: {噛|か}みしめます\n- Te-form: {噛|か}みしめて\n- Past: {噛|か}みしめた\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {喜|よろこ}びを{噛|か}みしめる: to savor one's joy\n- {言葉|ことば}を{噛|か}みしめる: to reflect on someone's words\n- {幸|しあわ}せを{噛|か}みしめる: to savor one's happiness\n- よく{噛|か}みしめて{食|た}べる: to chew well and eat",
